1 | devops | Fix issue 2747, which you must read in full first. THE PROBLEM, observed today and not theoretical: golangci/golangci-lint-action@v9 at .github/workflows/ci.yml line 205 runs golangci-lint config verify before it lints, and that step downloads the config JSON schema from the golangci-lint.run website on every single run. We do not set the verify input so it defaults to on. Go Lint is in the ci-passed needs list, which means every merge in this repo is gated on an external marketing website being reachable from a GitHub runner. It timed out on PR 2746 today, turned Go Lint red on a PR containing zero Go files, and a re-run with no other change passed immediately. YOUR TASK: remove the network dependency from the lint gate. FIRST establish the facts rather than assuming: read the golangci-lint-action v9 action.yml on the pinned ref to confirm what the input controlling config verification is actually called and whether it exists at all in v9. Do not guess at the input name from the issue text, which says to confirm it. If no such input exists, the fallback is to install and invoke the golangci-lint binary directly in a run step instead of going through the action, keeping the same version pin v2.11.4, the same working directory apps/api and the same timeout of 5m. THE TRAP TO AVOID, and this is the whole point of the task: do not trade a flake for a blind spot. Whatever you do must still fail the job when the config is genuinely invalid, and must still fail the job on a real lint violation. PROVE BOTH, do not assert them. In a THROWAWAY WORKTREE, commit a deliberately invalid apps/api/.golangci.yml, push that throwaway branch, and show the job failing. Then in a second throwaway commit introduce a real lint violation in a Go file and show the job failing on that too. Paste both failing run URLs. Commit before you break anything. Never run git stash, which is repo global, and never run git checkout to revert, which zeroes new files unrecoverably. Delete every throwaway branch afterwards and prove it with git ls-remote. Run make check-ci-wiring and paste the real exit code captured directly rather than read after a pipe. Confirm Go Lint remains in both the ci-passed and the report-main-red needs lists, since it must keep gating and keep paging. Keep the diff to .github/workflows/ci.yml unless the binary-install fallback genuinely requires more. Leave a comment in the workflow saying why verification is off, citing 2746, so nobody turns it back on next year without knowing what it cost. Open a PR with Closes 2747. Omit any Co-Authored-By trailer. Do not merge. | ci/2747-lint-no-network-dep

2 | backend-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the wave 1 change on branch ci/2747-lint-no-network-dep. You are not a producer: no commits, no push, no gh pr review, no gh pr merge, no labels, no test writing. The harness pushes the branch it checks out, so any commit on a producer ref is a production incident. Permitted writes are a slash tmp worktree only. Record the PR head SHA at start and re-check it at report time, and if it moved report BLOCKED with both SHAs. THE QUESTION THAT MATTERS: has the lint gate been quietly weakened. Turning off config verification is only safe if the linter still runs and still fails on real problems. A change that makes Go Lint green by making it do less is far worse than the flake it replaces, because a permanently green lint gate is invisible. VERIFY IN THIS ORDER. First, confirm the linter still actually executes and reports: read the step, and confirm no --issues-exit-code equal to zero, no continue-on-error, no exit code consumed by a pipe or a tee or a wrapper script, and no change to the linter set enabled in apps/api/.golangci.yml. The config file itself should be untouched by this diff, so flag any edit to it as suspicious and explain what it changes. Second, verify the two proofs are real by fetching both run URLs from the API rather than reading them from the PR body, and confirm each one failed in the Go Lint job specifically rather than somewhere else in the run. Confirm the invalid-config proof failed for a config reason and the lint-violation proof failed for a lint reason, since a proof that fails for the wrong reason proves nothing. Third, confirm no throwaway branch survives on the remote and that no part of either deliberate break leaked onto the task branch, by diffing the task branch against main. Fourth, confirm Go Lint is still present in both the ci-passed and the report-main-red needs lists in ci.yml, by parsing both lists rather than trusting the PR body. Fifth, confirm the version pin is still v2.11.4 and the working directory is still apps/api, because a silent version drift would change which linters run. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads CRITIC 2747 LINT NETWORK DEP, with a verdict of SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE, per-finding severity and file and line citations. No vendor names, emails, booking ids or gcloud payloads. | ci/2747-lint-no-network-dep
